<title>Suggested Algorithm for Lower Gastrointestinal Bleeding.</title>
<graphic href="eee0183-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Hematochezia. Initial evaluation, resuscitation, and stabilization.</label>
<path target="cell-2"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Nasogastric tube aspiration.</label>
<path target="cell-5">No blood</path>
<path target="cell-6">Blood</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Colonoscopy.</label>
<path target="cell-11">Source identified</path>
<path target="cell-12">Source not identified</path>
<path target="cell-13">Colonoscopy not possible</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Treat as indicated.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-12">
<label>Bleeding persists.</label>
<path target="cell-13">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-14">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-14">
<label>Small bowel studies.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-13">
<label>Radionuclide imaging.</label>
<path target="cell-15">Positive</path>
<path target="cell-17">Negative</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-17">
<label>Bleeding Persists.</label>
<path target="cell-15">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-18">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-18">
<label>Small bowel studies.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-15">
<label>Arteriography with embolization or vasopressin.</label>
<path target="cell-16"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-16">
<label>Surgical consultation.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>EGD.</label>
<path target="cell-5">Negative</path>
<path target="cell-7">Positive</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Upper GI source.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Adapted from Zuccaro G Jr. Management of the adult patient with acute lower gastrointestinal bleeding. American College of Gastroenterology. Practice Parameters Committee. <em>Am J Gastroenterol</em> 1998;<strong>93</strong>:1202&#x2013;1208.</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
